From: Patch — TCI mic-source auto-restore after PTT release
Subject: [PATCH] Add "auto-restore mic source after TCI PTT" option

Mixed voice + digital operation: when the operator has Mic source set to
"PC Soundcard (VAC1)" and a TCI client (WSJT-X, MSHV, SDRLogger+) drives
a digital transmission, Lyra auto-flips the picker to "TCI (digital modes)".
After PTT drops the picker stays on TCI — the microphone is silent until
the operator manually switches back.

This patch adds a persistent boolean preference
  tx/tci_restore_mic_source  (default false)
and a checkbox in Settings → TX → Audio + Gain:
  "Auto-restore mic source after TCI PTT release"

When enabled, Lyra records the mic-source token that was active *before*
the TCI keydown and restores it when:
  (a) the TCI client sends trx:0,false  (normal keyup), or
  (b) the txAudioOwner_ WebSocket disconnects while TX is active.

When disabled (default), behaviour is unchanged — operators running a
dedicated digital setup keep the current "stays on TCI" behaviour.

Files changed:
  src/prefs.h           — Q_PROPERTY, accessor, signal, private member
  src/prefs.cpp         — kTciRestoreMicSource constant, load, setter
  src/tci_server.h      — preMicSource_ member
  src/tci_server.cpp    — save-before-flip, restore-on-keyup/disconnect
  src/settingsdialog.cpp — checkbox widget wired to the new property

